---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/page/PageHero.astro';
import Band from '../components/ui/Band.astro';
import Prose from '../components/page/Prose.astro';
import { staticRow, org } from '../lib/page.js';

const row = staticRow({
  path: '/terms',
  pageType: 'core',
  title: 'Terms of Service | MrPackerMover',
  h1: 'Terms of service',
  metaDescription:
    'The terms governing quotes, bookings, payments, liability, claims and cancellations for moving services provided by MrPackerMover across India.',
  breadcrumbs: [{ path: '/', anchor: 'Home' }],
});
const o = org();
const legalName = o?.legalName ?? 'the Company';
---

<BaseLayout row={row}>
  <PageHero
    dark
    eyebrow="Legal"
    h1={row.h1}
    intro="The plain-language terms for using our website and moving services. We’ve kept them readable on purpose — you shouldn’t need a lawyer to understand what you’re agreeing to."
    breadcrumbs={row.breadcrumbs}
    current="Terms"
  />

  <Band label="Terms">
    <Prose>
      <div class="legal-notice">
        <strong>Draft for review.</strong> This template will be finalised with legal counsel before
        launch. The binding terms are those in force on the date you book. <span class="muted"
          >Effective date: to be set at launch.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who these terms are with</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are an agreement between you and <strong>{legalName}</strong> ({o?.brandName ??
        'MrPackerMover'}), a company registered in India{
          o?.gstin ? `, GSTIN ${o.gstin}` : ''
        }. By requesting a quote, booking a move, or using this website, you accept these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Our services</h2>
      <p>
        We provide packing, loading, transportation, unloading and related relocation services for
        homes and businesses in the areas we serve. We do not operate walk-in premises; services are
        delivered at your location and coordinated remotely.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Quotes, surveys and pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Quotes are prepared after a survey of your goods (in person or by video). A written,
        itemised quote is fixed for the scope it describes. If the scope changes — added items, or a
        service not originally quoted — we will confirm any revised charge with you before doing that
        work. Indicative prices shown on the site are for guidance only and are not a quote.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Bookings, payments and GST</h2>
      <p>
        A booking is confirmed against an accepted written quote and any token advance. The balance is
        payable on completion unless agreed otherwise. Applicable GST is shown as a line item, and a
        GST invoice is issued for every move.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give accurate details of your goods, locations, floors and access.</li>
        <li>Ensure lawful ownership of, and the right to move, all items handed to us.</li>
        <li>Personally carry cash, jewellery, documents and other high-value valuables.</li>
        <li>Declare hazardous, perishable or restricted items in advance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Items we cannot move</h2>
      <p>
        For safety and legal reasons we do not transport certain goods, including hazardous or
        flammable materials, illegal items, firearms and ammunition, and perishables, among others.
        The full list is confirmed at survey.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Care of your goods</h2>
      <p>
        We handle your goods with professional care, using a shared inventory and packing records.
        Despite this, transit carries inherent risk; sections 8 and 9 explain how liability and
        insurance work.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Liability and claims</h2>
      <p>
        Our liability for loss or damage caused by our handling is limited to the basic liability
        cover included with your move, unless you opt for transit insurance (section 9), in which case
        it extends to your declared insured value. We are not liable for pre-existing damage, items
        you packed yourself without our inspection, or losses outside our reasonable control. Claims
        must be raised within the window stated on your invoice and are handled as described on our
        <a href="/claims">claims page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Transit insurance</h2>
      <p>
        Transit insurance is optional and, when selected, is placed with a licensed insurer to your
        declared value. Cover, exclusions and the claims route are set out on our
        <a href="/insurance">insurance page</a> and in the policy certificate.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Cancellation, rescheduling and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You may cancel or reschedule; any token advance is refundable or adjustable subject to notice
        given and costs already incurred, as confirmed at booking. We may cancel where a move cannot
        be performed safely or lawfully, and will refund amounts not yet used.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Delays and events beyond control</h2>
      <p>
        We plan realistic timelines, but delays can arise from weather, traffic, strikes, regulatory
        checks or other events beyond our reasonable control. We are not liable for such delays but
        will keep you informed and work to minimise disruption.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Complaints and grievances</h2>
      <p>
        If something goes wrong, please tell us. Our process, response commitment and escalation route
        are on the <a href="/raise-a-complaint">raise-a-complaint</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Use of this website</h2>
      <p>
        The content, branding and design of this site are owned by {o?.brandName ?? 'MrPackerMover'}
        and may not be copied or used to impersonate us. Report any impersonation through our
        <a href="/fraud-check">fraud-check</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of India, and disputes are subject to the jurisdiction of
        the courts at the seat of our registered office.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The version in force when you book governs your
        move. Material changes will be posted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Reach us via the <a href="/company/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Band>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-notice {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-warn-500) 35%, var(--color-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-warn-500) 8%, white);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
  }
  .legal-notice strong {
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
  }
</style>
